      "sequence_position": 4,
      "problem": "The point $S$ is the midpoint of the line segment $\\overset{―}{PQ}.$ What is the value of $x$ if $SQ=x+9$ inches and $PS=2x+5$ inches?",
      "worked_solution": "We have the following diagram.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14171842/assets/29610a9e6bc2d25522c151c1676d438a860503e640bf9f7beb178ab73b3b6be7.png)\n\nSince $S$ is the midpoint of $\\overset{―}{PQ}$, the two segments $\\overset{―}{PS}$ and $\\overset{―}{SQ}$ have the same length. So, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}PS & =SQ \\\\ 2x+5 & =x+9 \\\\ 2x+5-x & =x+9-x \\\\ x+5 & =9 \\\\ x+5-5 & =9-5 \\\\ x & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $x=4\\,\\text{in}.$",
